.TH MX-GESTURE-DAEMON 1 "July 2026" "y5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mx\-gesture\-daemon \- Logitech MX Master gesture button daemon for Y5
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mx\-gesture\-daemon
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mx\-gesture\-daemon
listens to the gesture button of Logitech MX Master mice over hidraw
(HID++) and translates presses and directional gestures into actions in
a Y5 compositor session.
.PP
Device access is granted by the udev rule shipped as
.IR /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/42\-logitech\-hidpp.rules .
The daemon is started by the
.I mx\-gesture\-daemon.service
systemd user unit; enable it per user with
.B systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now mx\-gesture\-daemon.service
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mx\-gesture\-daemon/config.toml
Per-user configuration. A commented example is installed at
.IR /usr/share/y5\-compositor/mx\-gesture\-daemon/config.example.toml .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Log verbosity (standard
.BR env_logger (3)
syntax); the shipped unit sets
.BR info .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR y5.compositor (1)
